  "id": "5.2.172",
  "source": "CAT 1998 Q 12",
  "text": "Fill in the blanks of the following sentences using the most appropriate word or words.\n To a greater or lesser degree, all the civilised countries of the world are made up of a small class of rulers, _________ and of a\n large class of subjects, ___________\n A. Formed by a small minority, who are uncivilised.\n B. Powerfully corrupt, pointless crusaders.\n C. Corrupted by too much power, corrupted by too much passive obedience.\n D. Who are ruled, who ruled.",
